# nginx-external-body.yaml.in — body for unmask-nginx-external.
#
# For a host whose nginx no package installed -- built from source, by hand
# or by a hosting panel.  unmask-plugin-nginx and unmask-web-nginx depend on
# `nginx`, and there the package manager meets that by installing the
# distribution's nginx beside the one the host runs: a second nginx that
# takes the name on PATH (the package scripts then wire the wrong one) and
# may take the ports.  This package provides `nginx` and ships its
# documentation, nothing else: installed first, on purpose, it says that the
# host has an nginx already.
#
# No scripts, no dependencies, no files nginx reads.  What the other packages
# do with a self-built nginx is in rpm/scripts (the nginx-layout block).

description: |
  For a host whose nginx was built from source (by hand, or by a hosting
  panel).  Provides "nginx" to the package manager, so that
  unmask-plugin-nginx and unmask-web-nginx install without pulling in the
  distribution's nginx beside the one the host runs.  Install it first.
  It ships its documentation and nothing else; unmask edits nothing of such
  an nginx and names the two include lines to add to its nginx.conf.
  Not for a host whose nginx came from a package.

provides:
  - nginx

contents:
  - src: ./nginx-external/README
    dst: /usr/share/doc/unmask-nginx-external/README
    file_info:
      mode: 0644
  # Per-packager LICENSE entries: rpm marks it %license, deb and apk ship it
  # as a plain doc file (the other unmask packages do the same).
  - src: ../LICENSE
    dst: /usr/share/doc/unmask-nginx-external/LICENSE
    type: license
    packager: rpm
  - src: ../LICENSE
    dst: /usr/share/doc/unmask-nginx-external/LICENSE
    packager: deb
  - src: ../LICENSE
    dst: /usr/share/doc/unmask-nginx-external/LICENSE
    packager: apk
  - src: ../NOTICE
    dst: /usr/share/doc/unmask-nginx-external/NOTICE
  - src: ./conf/copyright
    dst: /usr/share/doc/unmask-nginx-external/copyright
    packager: deb
